===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[sound]] loudly, be [[amplified]]
#: {{ux|en|The music '''trumpeted''' from the speakers, hurting my ears.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[play]] the trumpet.
#: {{ux|en|Cedric made a living '''trumpeting''' for the change of passersby in the subway.}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} Of an elephant, to make its cry.
#: {{ux|en|The circus trainer cracked the whip, signaling the elephant to '''trumpet'''.}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To give a loud cry like that of an elephant.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Gerhard Gehrke|title=Nineveh's Child|passage=The bird '''trumpeted''' a second time. Dinah listened to the echo die around her.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[proclaim]] [[loudly]]; to promote [[enthusiastic]]ally
#: {{ux|en|Andy '''trumpeted''' Jane's secret across the school, much to her embarrassment.}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon War with Spain|passage=They did nothing but publish and '''trumpet''' all the reproaches they could devise against the Irish.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=31 Dec 77|volume=4|number=26|journal=Gay Community News|page=9|author=Sara Annie Fisher|title=Film Shows Women Victimized And Victorious|text=''One Sings, the Other Doesn't'' '''trumpets''' a gladsome triumph for feminists who have awaited the advent of unflinching women in film.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 2 2024|author=Howard LaFranchi; Anna Mulrine Grobe|titleurl=https://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Foreign-Policy/2024/0402/NATO-has-united-the-West-for-75-years.-Here-s-why-it-still-matters|title=NATO has united the West for 75 years. Here’s why it still matters.|journal=The Christian Science Monitor
|passage=An anniversary summit in Washington in July is sure to '''trumpet''' a nearly eight-decade record of success.}}

